    {
      "title": "NIA says Hafiz Saeed is in Pakistan, secures second warrant in 2 months",
      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/india-news/nia-says-hafiz-saeed-is-in-pakistan-secures-second-warrant-in-2-months-126091200201_1.html",
      "description": "LeT founder Hafiz Saeed, India's most-wanted terrorist, is in Pakistan, the NIA told a Special Court in Jammu, securing a second non-bailable warrant (NBW) against him in two months in connection with a terror case related to the supply of weapons, funds, and directions to terror groups operating in the Union Territory.\nThe court was hearing an application filed by the National Investigation Agency (NIA) seeking an NBW against Lashkar-e-Taiba (LeT) founder and designated terrorist under Section 75 of the Bharatiya Nagarik Suraksha Sanhita (BNSS).\nThe application described Saeed, a resident of Sargodha in Punjab (Pakistan), as an \"absconding accused\" in a case related to the arrest of Mohammad Naqeeb Bhat during a check at Pandach on the outskirts of Srinagar earlier in the year.\nA China-made grenade and 15 live rounds were recovered from Bhat, a resident of Batpora.\nBhat was booked at Zakoora Police Station under the UAPA, the Arms Act and the Explosive Substances Act.\nThe subsequ",
      "source_name": "Business Standard Latest",
      "published": "2026-09-12T05:53:58"
    }
